  "interpretation": [
    "At the post-Back pre-Quit snapshot, all three tails were fulfilled and projection outstanding was zero. The later sampled wait therefore arose after that snapshot, without identifying which intervening caller admitted it.",
    "After Quit, projection pending and gate tail were pending while storage tail remained fulfilled. This narrows the observed wait to work before storage or an unfinished gate lifetime; it does not establish a held Web Lock.",
    "PlayerProjectionPersistence.flush() enqueues but does not acquire the operation gate. A pending gate can belong to an accepted update or another shared gated operation ahead of the flush.",
    "Both dirty flags remained false. That is consistent with a wait before a guarded update merges, not proof that no write was accepted.",
    "Outstanding increased from 2 to 3, proving another accepted queue position but not its caller.",
    "The DOM paused observation was true after Back and false after Quit. The transition and its cause were not traced or diagnosed."
  ],
